  "result": "Gate verdict: **OK** (2 of 6 runs used).\n\n**What I wrote**\n\n- `library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_257_1_o1.lean` — the applicability from e1/c1/s1 (approach carrier selected by `rel.occupies` + `st.lane_enters` on the quantified intersection, a stop or yield sign governing that carrier, minus the officer/signal exception read on the junction or the carrier), and the obligation from ob1: judged at `drv.motion.region_entry`, the act found by `count actedAtPlace (¬(approachStarted ∨ entersIntersection)) ≥ 1`, with the place read in the words' order — stop line, else crosswalk, else the view point on the crossing way.\n- `library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_257_1_o1.lean` — 13 built witnesses on one map.\n\n**The two decisions worth your attention**\n\n1. The history-bounded search is written with `count`, not `since`. `since` evaluates its continuation condition at the judged observation, where the entry itself holds, so the previous-entry terminator would collapse the search onto that single instant. The cost — declared as a narrowing — is that the act is read at its onset, so an act already holding at the first observation after the search's end is not counted.\n2. The third place (\"the point nearest the intersection where the driver has a view\") has no region in a scene; it is read as an observation on the carrier where the sight along the crossing way reaches `p.intersecting_way_view_distance`, with \"nearest the intersection\" not read as a spatial minimum. Also declared.\n\nThree coder narrowings total, all on `ob1`; none on the trigger, condition or subject spans. The one gate failure was mine, in a witness: a final observation sat exactly on the approach lane's boundary, so occupancy of the carrier was not decided there and the duty went vacuous — moved 0.5 m inside. `task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
